  visitorName: tuto
  birthYear: 0
  birthMonth: 0
  birthDay: 0
  personality: here is personality
  note: when and where
  genuineGreeting: "Hey Ranger Navorksy, it\u2019s me, Ranger Frank. \nStorm winds
    are starting to pick up and they\u2019ve issued a park wide evacuation order.
    \nAnd since you have control over the remote exit gate you\u2019ve been tasked
    with vetting guests trying to exit the park. I\u2019m just stopping by to remind
    you how to use the tools in your station. \nGuests will be buzzing in over this
    intercom and asking to be let out of the park. \nIt's your job to question them
    and compare their information to the information on file and let them through
    the gate by hitting the flashing green button on your desk if it all matches
    up."
  mimicGreeting: Should not be mimic
  genuineClosing: "Remember to let guests through if all their information checks
    out. Otherwise, tell them to go away.\nBest of luck! Storm\u2019s really starting
    to brew it looks like it\u2019s gonna be one hell of a night.\r\n"
  mimicClosing: 0
  genuineRejected: "What are you doing, Navorsky? I\u2019m one of your own rangers!\r\n...Well,
    I suppose that proves you know how to reject someone, at least.\r\nJust make
    sure you\u2019re more careful when the real callers start coming through. \nCheck
    their files, listen closely, and don\u2019t let any Mimics through that gate.\r\nBest
    of luck. Storm\u2019s really starting to brew\u2014it looks like it\u2019s gonna
    be one hell of a night."
  mimicRejected: 0
  genuineNameResponse: "Click the monitor on your device to access your computer.
    Switch your view back at anytime by hitting the close button. \nHere you can
    access a lot of useful applications like mail, search, and the directory. \nMail
    provides some useful background information, check back regularly. Search can
    be used to type in the name of some websites you receive through emails or the
    directory. \nThe directory is your most important application which you will
    use to view information on visitors in the park. Compare information in the directory
    to answers the guests give you. \nIf all the info matches let them through the
    gate if not reject them."
  genuineBirthdayResponse: "When a call comes through the microphone on your desk
    will start blinking. Click it to pick up the call. \nThen question them on their
    name, Date of birth, arrival time, and reason for visiting and compare their
    answers to the information on file in the computer directory. \nAfter a while
    guests get impatient and will stop answering your questions so make sure you
    pay careful attention to their responses. The number of questions you have remaining
    can be viewed in the top right of your screen. \nAlso, remember to compare their
    personality to the description in their file as well."
  genuineReasonResponse: "Once you\u2019ve compared all of a quests answers to their
    file on the computer directory and checked the radio it\u2019s time to make a
    decision. \nIf everything was correct, hit the blinking green button on your
    desk to let guests through the gate. Don\u2019t press this button until your
    sure you want to let the guest through. \nIf there was an inconsistency with
    the information they gave and the information in the directory, their personality
    didn\u2019t match their file, an abnormality was detected on the radio or if
    they don\u2019t have a directory file, \ntell them to go away and do not allow
    them through the gate."
  genuineTimeResponse: "Sometimes a guest may appear to give all the right answers.
    But not so fast! \nMake sure to check your radio. Some anomalies only show up
    on the radio. \nClick on the radio to zoom in on it. Turn the knob on the radio
    to change between channels or turn it off. Make sure to check all the channels
    for any unusual static, pitch shifting, sounds or other irregularities."
  mimicNameResponse: 0
  mimicBirthdayResponse: 0
  mimicReasonResponse: 0
  mimicTimeResponse: 0
